{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions","id":1024085,"title":"On Playing a Metis: Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-29T20:38:35-08:00","id":1024085,"title":"On Playing a Metis: Questions","content":"Hello, everyone,<br /> <br /> This is my first time here and I am super excited to learn more about WtA and W20 from you all. I am a somewhat new player (I started a few years back, but stopped for a while, only recently getting back into the game in August 2016 when a friend introduced me to a new W20/VtM board). I play a Get of Fenris Metis Ahroun and he is the only Garou I have ever played. I love playing him, his personality, how he interacts with other characters, but I have had some difficulties IC because of things I wasn't aware of OOC as a player. I won't go into details, but let's just say I've made a few significant mistakes IC that made my character look like a manipulative douchebag because I wasn't entirely aware of all the options available when it comes to making peace after two Garou have had a spat (i.e. I tried to have my character apologize, but I never even thought of the Rite of Contrition, which was the more appropriate action to take).<br /> <br /> Also, one of our STs recently posted Ana Mizuki's &quot;What is a Metis?&quot; on our board (there are now 3 Metis on the board, including my character). I read it, but I felt that while that is one interpretation of how to play a Metis, it isn't the only one. There must be others. But I keep wondering in the back of my mind, am I playing this character right? Or am I giving him too human of a worldview? He has a deformity that allows him to live only on a caern/in the wild and never go into the city and he was raised by his human Kinfolk relatives, so I try to portray him as close to his wolf side and more unfamiliar with a lot of aspects of the human world, but he's also had an upbringing amongst Kinfolk, so he is aware of some things, he hunts and traps and fishes in Homid form as well as hunting as a wolf, etc.<br /> <br /> But his relationship with Garou society is really complicated. His parents are dead (instead of going with the Fenrir tribebook's scenario where the tribe forces the parents to raise the Metis, I went with the Sept killed the parents, although why exactly they went off script like that in that case I'm still trying to work out and I leave it vague). He was raised by his Kinfolk relatives, who he loves like they're his immediate family. He tends to have a grim atittude towards other Garou, but he does get along with individuals. He's a Fenrir Ahroun, so he's got the warrior image and trying to prove himself and rise above his breed thing going on. I'm still trying to figure out what would make him fight for the Garou Nation rather than against it since his home Sept killed his parents for being Litany-breakers (perhaps there was more going on than just giving birth to a Metis, though I know that is hugely significant). Anyway, for whatever reason, he's a loyal warrior of Gaia, even though he hates the Nation at times and his place in it. And he's just moved from his home Fenrir war sept to a multi-tribal Sept (the board's setting), so his horizons are slowly broadening.<br /> <br /> So, my questions are: How do you know you're doing it right or totally getting it wrong? Playing a Metis, I mean. And what do you do as a new player who is playing a character that grew up in and so should be totally familiar with Garou society, but you are not so familiar with it? Also, I struggle a lot with the hierarchy in Garou society. When an Elder treats him like shit, it just pisses me off, but there's nothing to be done since he's at the bottom. I understand I play a Metis and they'll get grief, but I feel like with the hierarchy those at the top can push around and abuse those at the bottom and there is no recourse. I know that's the nature of a hierarchy, but it just bothers me to my core. Also, can Metis rise above their birth and make something of themselves or is it a loss cause? From what I've read of W20, it sounds kind of mixed. Are they doomed to always be an omega and have to deal with abuse, even when they rise in rank? Is rising in rank a lot harder to accomplish when you play a Metis or does a Metis get to level up with Renown just like everyone else? I have no idea because I've only ever played him as a cliath. I've seen NPC Metis who are Adrens or Athros, but no Elders.<br /> <br /> It's late. I hope this made sense. Thank you in advance for answering my questions. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","user":"Ruadhan","date":". 12-29-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T20:51:58-08:00","id":1024088,"title":"","content":"Honestly how you play it is up to you and your crew.<br /> <br /> As for point two... With the Fenrir the shame is on the parents not the Metis. Metis can absolutely rise above. It varies from tribe to tribe, but Fenrir are specifically &quot;die gloriously&quot;. Check out tribe book revised for more on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T20:55:20-08:00","id":1024091,"title":"","content":"True that. Thanks! I should also mention he's left his home Sept, which was a Fenrir war sept, and gone to a multi-tribal Sept (the board's setting), so he's going to have to figure out how to get along with non-Fenrir. Right now everyone's mingling and he's getting along with a few people so far, but he's also supposed to be a bit of a jerk and not the easiest person to get along with. How do you balance that with not being stupid when it comes to pissing off other Garou/higher-ranked Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","user":"Ruadhan","date":". 12-29-2016, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T01:51:00-08:00","id":1024157,"title":"","content":"Honestly, one thing you need to remember with him being a Fenrir rather from any other tribe, is that his deeds are respected among his tribe and he gets treated equally as long as he keeps being strong. Him being an ahroun with no physical deformities is also a HUGE bonus for him. Of course, all of that comes from being put into the wringer multiple times to see if he'd crack. But he didn't, so he has every reason to be proud of himself and his tribe.<br /> <br /> About how you portray him, keep in mind that he still grew up in crinos and his knowledge of the world is painted with the perspective of his tribe. But, honestly, you are doing fine. The article's point was to note that metis are not just abused humans. Your character feels very real and fitting, worried about fighting the good fight.<br /> <br /> As for the abuse, I'd say view it through the Fenrir lens. Every beating, every insult and every right denied is just a test to pass. How can Terje defeat Wyrmspawn, if he cannot deal with his fellow garou being rough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T09:41:34-08:00","id":1024375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions#post1024085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my first time here and I am super excited to learn more about WtA and W20 from you all. I am a somewhat new player (I started a few years back, but stopped for a while, only recently getting back into the game in August 2016 when a friend introduced me to a new W20/VtM board). I play a Get of Fenris Metis Ahroun and he is the only Garou I have ever played. I love playing him, his personality, how he interacts with other characters, but I have had some difficulties IC because of things I wasn't aware of OOC as a player. I won't go into details, but let's just say I've made a few significant mistakes IC that made my character look like a manipulative douchebag because I wasn't entirely aware of all the options available when it comes to making peace after two Garou have had a spat (i.e. I tried to have my character apologize, but I never even thought of the Rite of Contrition, which was the more appropriate action to take).</div> </div> </div> </div>If what you did was get into a spat with a Garou or kin of equal or lesser rank, the Rite of Contrition is overkill. If you dishonored yourself or pissed off the Caern Totem, the Rite of Contrition is exactly the right thing to do. In between, it depends on the Tribes involved and the general tenor of the Sept. The Fenrir would probably laugh at the idea of performing a rite where a firm handshake will do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions#post1024085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my questions are: How do you know you're doing it right or totally getting it wrong? Playing a Metis, I mean. And what do you do as a new player who is playing a character that grew up in and so should be totally familiar with Garou society, but you are not so familiar with it? Also, I struggle a lot with the hierarchy in Garou society. When an Elder treats him like shit, it just pisses me off, but there's nothing to be done since he's at the bottom. I understand I play a Metis and they'll get grief, but I feel like with the hierarchy those at the top can push around and abuse those at the bottom and there is no recourse. I know that's the nature of a hierarchy, but it just bothers me to my core. Also, can Metis rise above their birth and make something of themselves or is it a loss cause? From what I've read of W20, it sounds kind of mixed. Are they doomed to always be an omega and have to deal with abuse, even when they rise in rank? Is rising in rank a lot harder to accomplish when you play a Metis or does a Metis get to level up with Renown just like everyone else? I have no idea because I've only ever played him as a cliath. I've seen NPC Metis who are Adrens or Athros, but no Elders.<br /> <br /> It's late. I hope this made sense. Thank you in advance for answering my questions. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know you're doing it right if you and the other players are having fun because of it. Circular logic, I know, but that's the way things go sometimes. The WoD setting is built to be inherently unfair and deliberately cruel to inexperienced characters. As a Metis player, you (presumably) signed up for a certain degree of abuse from the Sept Elders. If that turns out to not be your bag, you may want to consider talking to the GMs/other players about things you can do to resolve the &quot;let's shit on this particular Metis&quot; plot so you can go explore some other aspects of the game. Individual Metis can and do find ways to get the other Garou to rise above their prejudices. They usually rise in rank at similar rates to everyone else unless they do things that are particularly craven or leave their Sept particularly vulnerable to the Wyrm. Then they're unceremoniously put down &quot;for the greater good&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T12:20:24-08:00","id":1024446,"title":"","content":"Thank you both! Great advice! Ana Mizuki, I didn't know you were on the board! Who do you play on there? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T12:29:23-08:00","id":1024453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024446#post1024446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you both! Great advice! Ana Mizuki, I didn't know you were on the board! Who do you play on there?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eleazar, the nutcase Strider Metis.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you do good work with him and treat his deformity seriously ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T12:40:38-08:00","id":1024459,"title":"","content":"That's hilarious! I had you pegged for the other Strider Metis Red. Thank you! I'll try not to worry so much and just keep going as I am. Eleazar's great! I'm having fun interacting with him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T17:27:07-08:00","id":1024578,"title":"","content":"So you seemed to have gotten some good and useful answers already so I don't know how much can be added.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions#post1024085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, my questions are: How do you know you're doing it right or totally getting it wrong? Playing a Metis, I mean. And what do you do as a new player who is playing a character that grew up in and so should be totally familiar with Garou society, but you are not so familiar with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you were raised by kinfolk, so not being intimately familiar with Garou society can be excused if you fall back on that part of your backstory (how many dots of Rituals do you have?). Your home Caern can also play heavily into how your character expects to interact with Garou. And since you are in a new Sept, misunderstandings are bound to happen. If everyone has fun, you are doing well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions#post1024085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, I struggle a lot with the hierarchy in Garou society. When an Elder treats him like shit, it just pisses me off, but there's nothing to be done since he's at the bottom. I understand I play a Metis and they'll get grief, but I feel like with the hierarchy those at the top can push around and abuse those at the bottom and there is no recourse. I know that's the nature of a hierarchy, but it just bothers me to my core. Also, can Metis rise above their birth and make something of themselves or is it a loss cause? From what I've read of W20, it sounds kind of mixed. Are they doomed to always be an omega and have to deal with abuse, even when they rise in rank? Is rising in rank a lot harder to accomplish when you play a Metis or does a Metis get to level up with Renown just like everyone else? I have no idea because I've only ever played him as a cliath. I've seen NPC Metis who are Adrens or Athros, but no Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div> You'll gain renown like everyone else. The social interactions with higher ups and equals are just going to be rough. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> suggested, look at each and every difficulty as a test to be overcome. IC: You're Get. Act like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Nothing the other Garou can throw at you should dissuade you from proving yourself. To yourself, the spirits and to them. OOC: if it really gets to become to bothersome to you, talk to the ST ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar707_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"707\" data-vbnamecard=\"707\">etherial</a>'s suggestion).<br /> <br /> All in all, it sounds like you have a decent enough grasp on your character and the points your enjoying about him. That's a big portion of it.<br /> <br /> Oh...and Rite of Contrition is for big things. Not little spats. If you didn't battlescar your rival, you should be fine with an apology (even if they personally didn't accept it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:24:12-08:00","id":1024681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024578#post1024578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh...and Rite of Contrition is for big things. Not little spats. If you didn't battlescar your rival, you should be fine with an apology (even if they personally didn't accept it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the game, in some contrition is for big things. In some, it can be for apologizing for minor things if the person offended asks for it. Especially from a metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T07:32:24-08:00","id":1024752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024681#post1024681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the game, in some contrition is for big things. In some, it can be for apologizing for minor things if the person offended asks for it. Especially from a metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. That is just my experience with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:09:25-08:00","id":1024762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024752#post1024752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. That is just my experience with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the beauty of WtA at times, everyone plays a little differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:53:26-08:00","id":1024795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024578#post1024578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you seemed to have gotten some good and useful answers already so I don't know how much can be added.<br /> <br /> Well you were raised by kinfolk, so not being intimately familiar with Garou society can be excused if you fall back on that part of your backstory (how many dots of Rituals do you have?). Your home Caern can also play heavily into how your character expects to interact with Garou. And since you are in a new Sept, misunderstandings are bound to happen. If everyone has fun, you are doing well.<br /> <br /> You'll gain renown like everyone else. The social interactions with higher ups and equals are just going to be rough. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> suggested, look at each and every difficulty as a test to be overcome. IC: You're Get. Act like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Nothing the other Garou can throw at you should dissuade you from proving yourself. To yourself, the spirits and to them. OOC: if it really gets to become to bothersome to you, talk to the ST ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar707_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"707\" data-vbnamecard=\"707\">etherial</a>'s suggestion).<br /> <br /> All in all, it sounds like you have a decent enough grasp on your character and the points your enjoying about him. That's a big portion of it.<br /> <br /> Oh...and Rite of Contrition is for big things. Not little spats. If you didn't battlescar your rival, you should be fine with an apology (even if they personally didn't accept it).</div> </div> </div> </div>He's got 2 points in Rituals, but was raised by Kinfolk who lived on a caern. The Rite of Contrition and when to do it comments brings up another question: How do you know if you're in the setting where a Rite of Contrition should be done even for &quot;minor&quot; apologies or in one where it's only for major things? My use of the word &quot;spat&quot; might not have been the best. What actually happened is my character got into an argument with a Shadow Lord Kinswoman and made a threatening remark to her, which in hindsight I would have changed the wording since it was supposed to be him being a jerk, not actually threatening someone, which others saw as a Litany violation. Anyway, the Kinswoman made herself scarce at the Sept, so he couldn't find her to apologize. So he approached her Shadow Lord Garou handler (whatever you call the Garou responsible for a Kinfolk) to apologize and that guy got pissed and broke his nose. Time passed and then my Metis decided to challenge the Shadow Lord Garou to get it all resolved out in the open (or so I thought). So then the Master of Ceremonies and the Truthcatcher came and both thought all that was needed was for my character to do the Rite of Contrition to the Kinswoman and &quot;don't bring trivial shit like this to the mound again.&quot; So then I was like: Well, that makes sense. I should have thought of that, but I didn't know. I thought the Rite of Contrition was only between Garou, not a Garou and a Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Anyway, long story short, I'm just feeling really iffy on knowing what is the appropriate course to take or Rite to perform or whatever when it comes to tensions like this, especially since I play a Metis, so the worst will be thought of him when he screws up anyway. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","user":"Ruadhan","date":". 12-31-2016, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:30:18-08:00","id":1024905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024795#post1024795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's got 2 points in Rituals, but was raised by Kinfolk who lived on a caern. The Rite of Contrition and when to do it comments brings up another question: How do you know if you're in the setting where a Rite of Contrition should be done even for &quot;minor&quot; apologies or in one where it's only for major things? My use of the word &quot;spat&quot; might not have been the best. What actually happened is my character got into an argument with a Shadow Lord Kinswoman and made a threatening remark to her, which in hindsight I would have changed the wording since it was supposed to be him being a jerk, not actually threatening someone, which others saw as a Litany violation. Anyway, the Kinswoman made herself scarce at the Sept, so he couldn't find her to apologize. So he approached her Shadow Lord Garou handler (whatever you call the Garou responsible for a Kinfolk) to apologize and that guy got pissed and broke his nose. Time passed and then my Metis decided to challenge the Shadow Lord Garou to get it all resolved out in the open (or so I thought). So then the Master of Ceremonies and the Truthcatcher came and both thought all that was needed was for my character to do the Rite of Contrition to the Kinswoman and &quot;don't bring trivial shit like this to the mound again.&quot; So then I was like: Well, that makes sense. I should have thought of that, but I didn't know. I thought the Rite of Contrition was only between Garou, not a Garou and a Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Anyway, long story short, I'm just feeling really iffy on knowing what is the appropriate course to take or Rite to perform or whatever when it comes to tensions like this, especially since I play a Metis, so the worst will be thought of him when he screws up anyway. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, your character had every right to scare the kin if he wanted to. He is a Fenrir Ahroun and therefore a warrior of warriors, you do not want to anger one. Scaring a kin off is not violation of Respect all Beneath Ye, to violate that tenet you'd have to actually abuse and do harm to the kin physically.<br /> <br /> Second, the Lord handler's actions were fairly uncalled for. Kin, especially Lord kin, have to know their place and so her acting or causing trouble for your character would not be a good thing. Granted, the Lord could have beaten Terje to a pulp unofficially for scaring off the kin. But a single punch for the apology COULD be seen as Mound worthy for the Lord to not have taken care of their kin and lashing out to the wrong person.<br /> <br /> This is my own view, of course. The fact is that you don't know what kind of game you are in until you witness things yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:58:08-08:00","id":1024913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024905#post1024905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first off, your character had every right to scare the kin if he wanted to. He is a Fenrir Ahroun and therefore a warrior of warriors, you do not want to anger one. Scaring a kin off is not violation of Respect all Beneath Ye, to violate that tenet you'd have to actually abuse and do harm to the kin physically.<br /> <br /> Second, the Lord handler's actions were fairly uncalled for. Kin, especially Lord kin, have to know their place and so her acting or causing trouble for your character would not be a good thing. Granted, the Lord could have beaten Terje to a pulp unofficially for scaring off the kin. But a single punch for the apology COULD be seen as Mound worthy for the Lord to not have taken care of their kin and lashing out to the wrong person.<br /> <br /> This is my own view, of course. The fact is that you don't know what kind of game you are in until you witness things yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's very interesting. What I was told by other players is that Shadow Lords consider Kinfolk to fall under Respect the Territory of Another and that was the Litany tenet Terje broke, in addition to You Shall Not Eat the Flesh of Humans because of the wording of his threat. Let's just say the whole situation got milked for what it was worth by a lot of people on the board. Another Kinfolk even had the audacity to give Terje glaring, provacative looks after the Kinswoman had told him the story. Anyway, it was just a mess and I feel like I'm walking on eggshells as a new player. My character is more volatile, more the type to get into arguments or even fights about things, but at the same time, I don't want to go too far with that. My question is: Where are the limits here? If someone is insulting my character, what are his rights and what is an appropriate response? He's a Fenrir Ahroun, yes, but he's also Metis and it just feels like a lose-lose situation. Not that I want him going around and fighting with everyone. Of course not. I just need to know more of the nuances of responding to negative things that can happen between Garou. Know what I mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T09:26:19-08:00","id":1025081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024795#post1024795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's got 2 points in Rituals, but was raised by Kinfolk who lived on a caern. The Rite of Contrition and when to do it comments brings up another question: How do you know if you're in the setting where a Rite of Contrition should be done even for &quot;minor&quot; apologies or in one where it's only for major things?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rites Master of the Sept <i>tells you</i>. They're the one in charge of what Rites are appropriate when. If anyone else disagrees with them, too bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024795#post1024795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My use of the word &quot;spat&quot; might not have been the best. What actually happened is my character got into an argument with a Shadow Lord Kinswoman and made a threatening remark to her, which in hindsight I would have changed the wording since it was supposed to be him being a jerk, not actually threatening someone, which others saw as a Litany violation. Anyway, the Kinswoman made herself scarce at the Sept, so he couldn't find her to apologize. So he approached her Shadow Lord Garou handler (whatever you call the Garou responsible for a Kinfolk) to apologize and that guy got pissed and broke his nose. Time passed and then my Metis decided to challenge the Shadow Lord Garou to get it all resolved out in the open (or so I thought). So then the Master of Ceremonies and the Truthcatcher came and both thought all that was needed was for my character to do the Rite of Contrition to the Kinswoman and &quot;don't bring trivial shit like this to the mound again.&quot; So then I was like: Well, that makes sense. I should have thought of that, but I didn't know. I thought the Rite of Contrition was only between Garou, not a Garou and a Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the Rite of Contrition is being used to de-escalate a situation that had been repeatedly escalated. It would not have been called for in the original situation, though that may depend on why you were interacting with the SL Kinswoman in the first place and what the argument was about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024085-on-playing-a-metis-questions?p=1024795#post1024795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, long story short, I'm just feeling really iffy on knowing what is the appropriate course to take or Rite to perform or whatever when it comes to tensions like this, especially since I play a Metis, so the worst will be thought of him when he screws up anyway. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character is Cliath, right? They won't know what the right thing to do is anyway, so you (and your character) are learning through experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}